   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Shader Color Panels\n\nTranslucent color panels swing through depth and slide past each other: a glassy, architectural WebGL backdrop in any palette.\n\nCategory: shaders. Length: 5 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- You want an architectural, glassy backdrop of translucent panes sliding past each other.\n- A scene benefits from layered depth without organic blob motion; tune the panel count with `density`.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You want organic, flowing motion: use shader-warp or shader-metaballs.\n- The overlapping panes would clutter dense foreground content: lower `density`.\n- You need a single smooth gradient: use shader-mesh-gradient.\n\nVariables:\n- colors (string): Colors, default \"#3a3a52, #4a4a68, #52527a, #5a5a8a\"\n- color_back (color): Background, default \"#12121a\"\n- speed (number, 0-4): Speed, default 1\n- density (number, 1-8): Density, default 3\n- length (number, 0.5-3): Length, default 1.1\n- blur (number, 0-0.5): Blur, default 0\n- gradient (number, 0-1): Gradient, default 0\n- rotation (number, 0-360): Rotation, default 0\n- scale (number, 0.1-4): Scale, default 0.8\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.5\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
